{"w":2400,"h":3106,"lines":[{"y":0.074050225514057599,"h":0.016097875080489321,"t":"Test 2","x":0.15977443587673254,"w":0.058270676930745446,"c":1},{"x":0.15977443026046009,"t":"READING PASSAGE 2","w":0.29699249267578121,"y":0.12202189316113843,"c":1,"h":0.018995492594977459},{"w":0.78958160400390631,"c":1,"y":0.16111838592650152,"x":0.15971440239109852,"h":0.021174603405109349,"t":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14-26, which are based on Reading"},{"w":0.16353383382161454,"y":0.17868641351995351,"t":"Passage 2 below.","x":0.1578947370932762,"h":0.018995492594977459,"c":1},{"t":"Oxytocin","h":0.023255814296233579,"y":0.21947674399390982,"c":1,"x":0.49436090434717606,"w":0.12781954447428379},{"c":1,"x":0.16721061175808483,"y":0.25576432414348838,"w":0.78780975341796866,"t":"The positive and negative effects of the chemical known as the 'love hormone'","h":0.024099351203756392},{"t":"A Oxytocin is a chemical, a hormone produced in the pituitary gland in the brain. It","x":0.15789473445379704,"y":0.29651162806156228,"w":0.76879699707031257,"h":0.020348836895119238,"c":1},{"w":0.74448679606119794,"y":0.31525820755658507,"x":0.20294427517364833,"c":1,"t":"was through various studies focusing on animals that scientists first became aware","h":0.020775352227480504},{"t":"of the influence of oxytocin. They discovered that it helps reinforce the bonds","h":0.019349750978134517,"c":1,"x":0.20107542101373382,"y":0.33383729254991834,"w":0.69372283935546886},{"y":0.35465116265972529,"x":0.20112782518732503,"w":0.70300750732421879,"h":0.017531709370118831,"c":1,"t":"between prairie voles, which mate for lite, and triggers the motherly behaviour"},{"y":0.37209302312474191,"c":1,"w":0.7048872375488282,"h":0.017475553734872085,"x":0.2011278097090578,"t":"that sheep show towards their newborn lambs. It is also released by women in"},{"w":0.74444554646809902,"h":0.019456461791599211,"t":"childbirth, strengthening the attachment between mother and baby. Few chemicals","y":0.38943802991355247,"c":1,"x":0.20108613164950631},{"h":0.016097875080489432,"c":1,"t":"have as positive a reputation as oxytocin, which is sometimes referred to as the","y":0.40985189937574362,"x":0.20112781849731087,"w":0.71616541544596357},{"t":"'love hormone'. One sniff of it can, it is claimed, make a person more trusting,","x":0.19913053109182233,"y":0.42512513063318758,"h":0.021812127009561921,"c":1,"w":0.70137649536132818},{"x":0.20108378946511485,"c":1,"y":0.44616953013122007,"h":0.020151498159591608,"w":0.71061879475911471,"t":"empathetic, generous and cooperative. It is time, however, to revise this wholly"},{"t":"optimistic view. A new wave of studies has shown that its effects vary greatly","y":0.46511627893871754,"x":0.20112782194228468,"w":0.68796991984049471,"h":0.017498015743336648,"c":1},{"y":0.48250315339505745,"x":0.20109216149045872,"h":0.021326916185564482,"c":1,"t":"depending on the person and the circumstances, and it can impact on our social","w":0.72378397623697921},{"x":0.19917106684745467,"h":0.016510008537454546,"t":"interactions for worse as well as for better.","w":0.3855049641927083,"y":0.50097653488487592,"c":1},{"w":0.016917292277018214,"c":1,"h":0.013081395234588733,"t":"C","x":0.15601503797803226,"y":0.77906976740554623},{"t":"Oxytocin's role in human behaviour first emerged in 2005. In a groundbreaking","w":0.70676691691080729,"h":0.017707662588538398,"x":0.20112781421376941,"y":0.53766902744252121,"c":1},{"w":0.70876922607421866,"c":1,"h":0.020467601586984796,"y":0.55514120343513318,"x":0.20107553608029519,"t":"experiment, Markus Heinrichs and his colleagues at the University of Freiburg,"},{"y":0.57558139521807739,"w":0.74060150146484371,"h":0.017464322730639692,"c":1,"t":"Germany, asked volunteers to do an activity in which they could invest money with","x":0.20112782060240494},{"x":0.20101520565574418,"t":"an anonymous person who was not guaranteed to be honest. The team found","h":0.020636989006440398,"c":1,"y":0.59175160117928716,"w":0.70137308756510408},{"w":0.72180450439453125,"h":0.017508310881723332,"t":"that participants who had sniffed oxytocin via a nasal spray beforehand invested","c":1,"x":0.20112782288135292,"y":0.61191860451931734},{"x":0.20112782763508968,"t":"more money than those who received a placebo instead. The study was the start","y":0.6307147454229034,"w":0.72744359334309916,"c":1,"h":0.017541068642659807},{"w":0.72387044270833334,"h":0.021801963899493293,"c":1,"t":"of research into the effects of oxytocin on human interactions. 'For eight years, it","x":0.20104185755312395,"y":0.64581189072772749},{"c":1,"t":"was quite a lonesome field,' Heinrichs recalls. 'Now, everyone is interested.' These","y":0.66548846832364039,"x":0.2010557641039219,"w":0.74262420654296879,"h":0.022005625256245498},{"y":0.68471848823674009,"h":0.02069069444173699,"c":1,"t":"follow-up studies have shown that after a sniff of the hormone, people become","w":0.70690928141276044,"x":0.19917545107740656},{"x":0.20112782062370929,"c":1,"y":0.70494186033368944,"w":0.74060150146484383,"t":"more charitable, better at reading emotions on others' faces and at communicating","h":0.017530773504273234},{"w":0.70676691691080729,"h":0.017518606020110128,"y":0.72376046387320225,"x":0.20112781965641546,"t":"constructively in arguments. Together, the results fuelled the view that oxytocin","c":1},{"c":1,"h":0.016121273568884709,"y":0.74273255786522319,"t":"universally enhanced the positive aspects of our social nature.","x":0.20112782690904565,"w":0.56390975952148437},{"w":0.72744359334309894,"c":1,"y":0.77906976731084643,"h":0.017453091726407521,"t":"Then, after a few years, contrasting findings began to emerge. Simone Shamay-","x":0.19924812803792719},{"c":1,"h":0.017707662588538287,"t":"Tsoory at the University of Haifa, Israel, found that when volunteers played a","x":0.20112782193827211,"w":0.68796991984049471,"y":0.79781068907228303},{"x":0.2011278229022806,"w":0.72180450439453125,"h":0.017496144011645454,"y":0.81680618169569907,"t":"competitive game, those who inhaled the hormone showed more pleasure when","c":1},{"c":1,"x":0.19924813701865049,"t":"they beat other players, and felt more envy when others won. What's more,","w":0.68045110066731762,"y":0.83419188640356423,"h":0.017707662588538287},{"c":1,"t":"administering oxytocin also has sharply contrasting outcomes depending on a","x":0.20107047718778623,"h":0.019171585824822812,"y":0.8517954370725338,"w":0.69935796101888026},{"h":0.017508310881723332,"y":0.87057308459297644,"c":1,"x":0.20112780970762817,"t":"person's disposition. Jennifer Bartz from Mount Sinai School of Medicine, New","w":0.7048872375488282},{"x":0.20105073290461292,"w":0.72006952921549472,"y":0.88660074788797083,"h":0.022351998785427929,"c":1,"t":"York, found that it improves people's ability to read emotions, but only if they are"},{"y":0.90843023242680587,"c":1,"w":0.73872182210286452,"x":0.20112781067480853,"h":0.017519542500040841,"t":"not very socially adept to begin with. Her research also shows that oxytocin in fact"},{"h":0.017529837638427526,"x":0.19924813167925048,"t":"reduces cooperation in subjects who are particularly anxious or sensitive","w":0.65601501464843759,"y":0.92723760434787528,"c":1},{"w":0.11090225219726563,"t":"to rejection.","h":0.0161100419505672,"y":0.9462209304420669,"c":1,"x":0.19924812222530203},{"t":"42","x":0.15413533837736315,"y":0.98255813953750226,"w":0.026315789222717267,"h":0.013081395234588733,"c":1}]}